# The scene builder's clang-tidy config (D2w): native/.clang-tidy (cppcoreguidelines,
# bugprone, performance, modernize — every warning an error) plus this
# directory's headers, minus the checks below, each disabled for a stated reason.
#
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index
#       operator[] on std::vector / std::array. buildSnapshot, snapshotToFrameScene
#       and the effect packers are ported line for line from src/core/rendering
#       and packages/renderer so they stay reviewable against the TS; indices are
#       loop-bounded by the container's own size or fixed by the uniform layouts.
#       ASan (the sanitizer presets) covers them at runtime.
#   modernize-use-designated-initializers
#       Pt / Rgba / Mat3 / LayerError are value tuples mirroring the TS object
#       literals; naming every field at each site doubles the line without
#       catching anything the distinct types do not already catch.
#   bugprone-branch-clone
#       The ports keep the TS's branch structure (the effect switch has cases
#       with identical bodies) so a diff against the TS stays readable.
#   readability-function-cognitive-complexity
#       buildNode / layerToRenderable / the effect packers are single long
#       functions in the TS; splitting them would break the one-to-one reading
#       the parity gate relies on.
#   bugprone-float-loop-counter, clang-analyzer-security.FloatLoopCounter
#       The TS accumulates sample positions in float loop counters (flattenOutline,
#       Offset Paths); the same accumulation is what lands the same points.
#   cppcoreguidelines-avoid-const-or-ref-data-members
#       BuildContext and the snapshot walk are views over ONE frame's inputs (the
#       document, the editor view, the expression env) for the duration of one
#       call; reference members say exactly that and forbid reseating.
#   clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding
#       RLayer mirrors the TS RenderLayer's field order so the port reads against
#       it; the snapshot holds a few hundred per frame, so the padding is noise.
Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-const-or-ref-data-members,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding,
  -modernize-use-designated-initializers,
  -bugprone-branch-clone,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -bugprone-float-loop-counter,
  -clang-analyzer-security.FloatLoopCounter
InheritParentConfig: true
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*(native[/\\](include|libs)|scene)[/\\].*'
